 R←Test_UC_028(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;buff;stop;C
⍝ Runs ]StashPush with "?", which lets the user pick what to stash. The test was "¯1≢ind" rather
⍝ than "¯1≡ind", so every genuine selection was reported as "Cancelled by user" and nothing was
⍝ ever stashed; a real quit indexed list[¯1;] instead. The selected paths were also taken from
⍝ column 2 (the status letters) rather than column 3.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 stop←0

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 (⊂' r←Counter' ' r←4711')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/APLSource/Counter.aplf')1
 (⊂'# APLGit2 test project' '' 'Changed as well')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/README.md')1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠≢0 1 G.Status tempDir          ⍝ Two modified files to choose from

 C←∆GetRefToCommTools
 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'SelectForStash@' 1     ⍝ Take the first one

 (rc msg buff)←stop ∆UCMD'StashPush "',tempDir,'" ?'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/'Cancelled'⍷∊buff
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢G.StashList tempDir           ⍝ Something was stashed ...
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢0 1 G.Status tempDir          ⍝ ... and exactly one file was left alone

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 C.Cleanup
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
